Z||000000||Rodrv6||01-26-2001||10:12 PM||||Well, I finally went and bought another Fiero.  I found a white 88 GT today at a local used car dealer that was too good to pass up!  It has 134,000 miles and is in good solid ORIGINAL condition (no mods).  It is in need of some tender loving care, but seems to be a good car.  Tomorrow I'll be doing a tune up and oil change and starting a list of things to start getting to make it into a very sweet car.  Mostly interior stuff (steering wheel, seat covers, floor mats and such) and a replacement trunk lock.  The original is missing and using a screwdriver to get the trunk open is already getting old.  <BR>Now I don't know what to do with my black 84.<BR>I've had it since new and have enjoyed all 331,000 miles I've put on her.  I really can't justify having 4 cars with only one driver, but I guess I'll keep her for now. The other cars are a Nissan Maxima (daily driver and useful for when I want to carry more than one other person) and a 66 Porsche 911 (my other toy and WAY too much fun to sell).<BR>Also, could someone give me the name of the person who was collecting data on 88 GT's.  I'd like to send him the VIN and any other info he would like to have.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting :)||||reg||6
